        <item>
            <title>1.2.3</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:15:36 -0400</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.2.3</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.2.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Draw on a screenshot after you take it

After a screenshot, the "Screenshot saved" note at the top of the screen now
shows a small picture of it and says **right ⌘ to mark up**. Tap right ⌘ while
it is there and the shot opens ready to draw on, with no trip through the
panel. Clicking the note does the same, and it stays put while your pointer is
over it. Once it is gone, right ⌘ opens Cubby as always.

How long it stays is up to you, in **Settings → Screenshots**: off, or 3 to 15
seconds. Missed it? **Mark Up Last Screenshot** is in the menu bar menu.

### Paste it straight from the editor

When you have finished drawing, **⌘↩** pastes the marked-up picture straight
into the app you were in. **Done** still only copies it, so nothing pastes
unless you ask. Screenshot, right ⌘, draw, ⌘↩, and it is in your message.

### Find pictures by kind and day

Type **gif**, **video** or **shot** in the search to see only those, and
**today**, **yesterday** or a day like **monday** to see what you took then.
They combine with each other and with ordinary search: **shot yesterday
login** finds yesterday's screenshots with "login" in them. Press **?** in the
panel for the full list.
]]></description>
